Z||000000||Cozmo||06-04-2001||07:50 AM||||I'm usually quite sensible and responsible,  but after a weekend of fine tuning the Targa I was susceptible to temptation...<BR>Driving home at dusk yesterday, I stopped at a red light and was enjoying the nice exhaust burble and the fresh air when lo and behold...look what pulls up next to me...<BR>BIG winged fart canned bright yellow Toyota Supra!  We eyed each other, the "secret nod" was passed, and when the light changed we both thumped it! (3 lane empty straight  road, I'm still THAT sensible <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">)<BR>  I got the jump on him, 1/2 car length through first gear, then when I went to second he caught up and we were dead even.  It was funny...I wound it out to 5500 in second, he must have shifted second through fourth while I was still in second!  I slowly extended a car length lead on him and was still gaining when we shut it down.  He was very cool, at the next light he gave a "thumbs up", smiled and said "that Fiero sounds pretty mean!"<BR>  I guess this shows that all the stereotypes we joke about here aren't always true.  This guy acted very civil.<BR>  Needless to say, the Targa got a nice little pat on the roof when she got home to the garage...<BR>Woo-Woo <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"><BR><B>C02M0</B><BR>||||reg||6
Z||000001||mrfixit58||06-04-2001||07:53 AM||||WAY TO GO, COSMO! I glad to hear you've got all the little bugs out. <P>See ya,<P>------------------<BR>Roy :D<BR>87 GT  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG"> ||||reg||14
